title: coding-router tier selection
---
sequenceDiagram
  %% Source for 11-coding-router-flow.html. Edit this file, then run ./scripts/render-diagrams.py.
  %% Directives: docs in diagrams/README.md (Updating diagrams).
  %% @subtitle Keywords or D3-mini pick the tier; only the classification request leaves for the remote D3-mini host
  %% @type external: D3 EUP
  actor C as Client
  participant AR as LiteLLM Auto Router<br/>model = coding-router
  participant D3 as D3-mini<br/>remote GPU host
  participant EUP as Regional model provider<br/>tier models from .env

  C->>AR: chat completion for coding-router
  alt prompt matches CODING_ROUTER_<TIER>_KEYWORDS
    Note over AR: tier set by the keyword, no classification
  else session pinned (CODING_ROUTER_SESSION_AFFINITY)
    Note over AR: reuse the model the session's first turn chose
  else classify
    AR->>D3: classification request only
    alt D3 answers within CODING_ROUTER_CLASSIFIER_TIMEOUT_MS
      D3-->>AR: tier SIMPLE, MEDIUM, COMPLEX, or REASONING
    else timeout or error
      D3--xAR: no answer in time
      Note over AR: local heuristic scores the prompt
    end
  end
  Note over AR: pick a model from the tier's pool (random or adaptive),<br/>moving up a tier if the prompt or an image does not fit
  AR->>EUP: original request to the chosen model
  EUP-->>AR: completion
  AR-->>C: response
